<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <item>
      type        : CONFIG_CHECK
      description : "Check for MPLS"
      item        : "mpls ldp"
    </item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <item>
          type        : CONFIG_CHECK
          description : "loopback"
          context     : "interface @MPLS_LOOPBACK_INTERFACE@"
          item        : "ip address @MPLS_LOOPBACK_IP@ [^ ]+"
        </item>

        <item>
          type        : CONFIG_CHECK
          description : "mpls router-id"
          context     : "mpls ldp"
          item        : "router-id @MPLS_LOOPBACK_IP@"
        </item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.60 CISC-RT-000590"
          info        : "The Cisco MPLS router must be configured to use its loopback address as the source address for LDP peering sessions.

GROUP ID: V-216787RULE ID: SV-216787r991936

Using a loopback address as the source address offers a multitude of uses for security, access, management, and scalability of backbone routers. It is easier to construct appropriate ingress filters for router management plane traffic destined to the network management subnet since the source addresses will be from the range used for loopback interfaces instead of from a larger range of addresses used for physical interfaces. Log information recorded by authentication and syslog servers will record the router's loopback address instead of the numerous physical interface addresses."
          solution    : "Configure the router to use their loopback address as the source address for LDP peering sessions. As noted in the check content, the default behavior is to use its loopback address.

RP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config)#mpls ldp router-id 10.1.1.1"
          reference   : "800-53|CP-8,800-53r5|SC-47,CAT|III,CCI|CCI-004931,CSF|ID.BE-4,CSF|PR.PT-4,CSF2.0|PR.IR-04,GDPR|32.1.b,GDPR|32.1.c,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(ii),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.29,ISO-27001-2022|A.7.11,ITSG-33|CP-8,ITSG-33|CP-8a.,LEVEL|3M,NESA|T2.2.4,NESA|T4.5.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216787r991936_rule,STIG-ID|CISC-RT-000590,Vuln-ID|V-216787"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23599"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>
    </if>
  </then>

  <else>
    <report type:"PASSED">
      description : "1.60 CISC-RT-000590"
      info        : "The Cisco MPLS router must be configured to use its loopback address as the source address for LDP peering sessions.

GROUP ID: V-216787RULE ID: SV-216787r991936

Using a loopback address as the source address offers a multitude of uses for security, access, management, and scalability of backbone routers. It is easier to construct appropriate ingress filters for router management plane traffic destined to the network management subnet since the source addresses will be from the range used for loopback interfaces instead of from a larger range of addresses used for physical interfaces. Log information recorded by authentication and syslog servers will record the router's loopback address instead of the numerous physical interface addresses."
      solution    : "Configure the router to use their loopback address as the source address for LDP peering sessions. As noted in the check content, the default behavior is to use its loopback address.

RP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config)#mpls ldp router-id 10.1.1.1"
      reference   : "800-53|CP-8,800-53r5|SC-47,CAT|III,CCI|CCI-004931,CSF|ID.BE-4,CSF|PR.PT-4,CSF2.0|PR.IR-04,GDPR|32.1.b,GDPR|32.1.c,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(ii),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.29,ISO-27001-2022|A.7.11,ITSG-33|CP-8,ITSG-33|CP-8a.,LEVEL|3M,NESA|T2.2.4,NESA|T4.5.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216787r991936_rule,STIG-ID|CISC-RT-000590,Vuln-ID|V-216787"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23599"
    </report>
  </else>
</if>

<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <item>
      type        : CONFIG_CHECK
      description : "Check for MPLS"
      item        : "mpls ldp"
    </item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <item>
          type        : CONFIG_CHECK
          description : "Check for OSPF"
          item        : "router ospf"
        </item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <item>
          type        : CONFIG_CHECK
          description : "1.61 CISC-RT-000600"
          info        : "The Cisco MPLS router must be configured to synchronize IGP and LDP to minimize packet loss when an IGP adjacency is established prior to LDP peers completing label exchange.

GROUP ID: V-216788RULE ID: SV-216788r531087

Packet loss can occur when an IGP adjacency is established and the router begins forwarding packets using the new adjacency before the LDP label exchange completes between the peers on that link. Packet loss can also occur if an LDP session closes and the router continues to forward traffic using the link associated with the LDP peer rather than an alternate pathway with a fully synchronized LDP session. The MPLS LDP-IGP Synchronization feature provides a means to synchronize LDP with OSPF or IS-IS to minimize MPLS packet loss. When an IGP adjacency is established on a link but LDP-IGP synchronization is not yet achieved or is lost, the IGP will advertise the max-metric on that link."
          solution    : "Configure the MPLS router to synchronize IGP and LDP, minimizing packet loss when an IGP adjacency is established prior to LDP peers completing label exchange.

OSPF Example

RP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config)#router ospf 1RP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config-ospf)#mpls ldp syncRP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config-ospf)#end

IS-IS Example

RP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config)#router isis 1RP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config-isis)#interface g0/0/0/1RP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config-isis-if)#address-family ipv4 unicastRP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config-isis-if-af)#mpls ldp syncRP/0/0/CPU0:R3(config-isis-if-af)#end"
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|III,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|3M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216788r531087_rule,STIG-ID|CISC-RT-000600,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-216788"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23599"
          context     : "router ospf"
          item        : "mpls ldp sync"
        </item>
      </then>

